      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T07:58:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The close-order change isn\u0027t needed for the reconnection fix itself. It fixes two other things:\n\n- Cleanup skipped on error: SessionManagerImpl#closeSession() throws a RuntimeException when the channel doesn\u0027t shut down in time. With the session closed first, that exception skipped closing the status listener. The listener stayed active and the removed node\u0027s node-state stayed in the operational datastore. In the initializer it also skipped cancelling the pending connection.\n\n- Late status writes: closing the listener first switches it off. The SHUTDOWN caused by closing the channel is no longer written only to be deleted. A late READY from a reconnect is now rejected instead of written for a node that is being removed; that READY callback can only happen now because it stays registered.",
      "parentUuid": "d489a2a3_6b6bb9e8",
      "revId": "eb22bc0598817cd0c8dc0ad174613dd8b6d7ffe5",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
